@*
    The default price on a product or a service form.

    Administrators type in it. Staff see it, greyed and locked, with a line
    saying why - a disabled field with no explanation reads as a fault in the
    system, and someone then goes looking for a way around it.

    Locking it here is a courtesy, not the control. A read-only input still
    posts its value and a form can be replayed, so the controllers drop the
    posted price for anyone who may not set it; see AdminOnlyPriceAttribute.
*@
@{
    var canEdit = ViewData["CanEditPrice"] as bool? ?? false;
    var value = ViewData["PriceValue"] as string;
    var field = ViewData["PriceField"] as string ?? "DefaultPrice";
}

@if (canEdit)
{
    <input name="@field" value="@value" type="number" step="0.01" min="0" class="form-control" />
}
else
{
    <input value="@value" type="number" step="0.01" class="form-control" disabled
           aria-describedby="priceLocked" />
    <div class="form-text" id="priceLocked">
        <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="vertical-align:-1px;margin-right:3px"><rect width="18" height="11" x="3" y="11" rx="2" /><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4" /></svg>
        Prices are set by an administrator. You can still type a different
        price on an individual line when you quote or invoice.
    </div>
}
